## Required tests and falsification

Add focused tests that prove at least:

1. the registered route-and-mount surface equals the corrected contract, and a
   new undeclared `Route` or `Mount` fails the guard;
2. `/static/` permits `GET` and `HEAD`, refuses mutation methods appropriately,
   and serves only the approved root;
3. traversal attempts, encoded traversal, missing files and directory requests
   cannot expose content, directory listings, exception text or filesystem
   paths;
4. untrusted hosts remain refused on static requests;
5. static assets remain reachable during the portal kill switch while protected
   application routes retain their accepted kill-switch behavior;
6. static responses set the accepted cache policy and do not set or refresh
   authentication/session/CSRF cookies;
7. `ConfirmScope` and `CharacterFilters` match the corrected contract exactly;
8. VM-13 carries server-rendered CSRF and R-37 still rejects missing or invalid
   tokens;
9. R-36 returns the accepted `200` denied VM-13 response and never redirects;
10. every generic denial uses `DeniedView`, while the non-member page retains
    its separate VM-02 behavior;
11. denied-object and absent-object `404` bodies remain byte-identical, with no
    correlation, UUID, guild name, timestamp or object detail;
12. direct unauthorized calls remain denied before object lookup where required;
13. template/static structural guards still prove zero unsafe Jinja `|safe`,
    `hx-on:`, inline executable script, CDN, remote-font and
    `design-prototype/` production references; and
14. the complete existing portal and bot suites remain green.

Include falsification evidence for the mount inventory guard and denial leakage
guard: demonstrate that each test fails when its protected defect is
